# Kept out of the distributed package. `src`, `config`, `database`, `lang`,
# `stubs` and `resources` are what an application installs; everything else is
# how this repository is developed.
#
# `package.json` is deliberately NOT in this list, however much it looks like
# a development file. `FrontendRequirements::npmPackages()` reads it at
# runtime, from inside `vendor/`, to tell an application which npm packages
# the published components import. Export-ignoring it did not make
# `panel:install` complain — it made the check return an empty list, so the
# installer reported no missing dependencies because it could not look. The
# one command whose job is to say what is missing said nothing was.
/.github            export-ignore
/.ai                export-ignore
/.claude            export-ignore
/.codex             export-ignore
/docs               export-ignore
/examples           export-ignore
/integration        export-ignore
/tests              export-ignore
# `frontend/browser` and `frontend/entry.ts` are how this repository builds and
# browser-tests itself. `frontend/host` is not: it is the minimal stand-in for
# each of the nineteen modules the published components import and do not ship,
# and `panel:install` copies the ones a blank application has none of. It used
# to be export-ignored with the rest, which meant an application with no starter
# kit got a build error and a list of nineteen files to write by hand.
/frontend/browser   export-ignore
/frontend/entry.ts  export-ignore
/.editorconfig      export-ignore
/.gitattributes     export-ignore
/.gitignore         export-ignore
/CHANGELOG.md       export-ignore
/phpstan.neon       export-ignore
/phpunit.xml        export-ignore
/pint.json          export-ignore
/package-lock.json  export-ignore
/tsconfig.json      export-ignore
/vite.config.ts     export-ignore
/vitest.config.ts   export-ignore
/eslint.config.js   export-ignore
/.prettierrc.json   export-ignore
/.prettierignore    export-ignore
